# Trivy ignore file — accepted CVEs per
# KNOWLEDGE-BASE/CONTEXT/PATTERNS/common/accept-with-rationale.md §
# "Entries from `trivy-prescan-2026-05-11`".
#
# Each entry is a CVE-ID, one per line. Trivy's CLI + Action both honour this
# file at the scan-context root.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-08-10 — THE TECH-DEBT BLOCK IS PAID OFF, NOT RE-ACCEPTED.
#
# From 2026-05-11 to today this file also carried 14 *fixable* CVEs
# grandfathered across three rounds ("bumping ALL affected files is
# out-of-scope for this branch"). Each round deferred the same work to "the
# next fleet-wide deps bump sprint", and the gate stayed red anyway on newer
# findings — so the suppressions bought nothing and hid a moving target.
#
# All 14 were resolved by ACTUALLY BUMPING, in one fleet-wide pass:
#   postcss  ^8.5.10 → ^8.5.18  (13 product/template frontends)
#            + the EXACT `"overrides": {"postcss": "8.5.10"}` pin in
#              seed/lib/frontend + seed/framework/frontend, which is what
#              froze the whole fleet on a 3-month-old postcss.
#   nanoid   3.3.11/3.3.12/3.3.16 → 3.3.18 (transitive via postcss; the
#            postcss bump carries it everywhere except orbity, which needed
#            an explicit `npm update nanoid`).
#   brace-expansion 2.x → ^2.1.4 via a VERSION-SCOPED override
#            (`"brace-expansion@^2.0.0"`), in erp-imobiliario/frontend +
#            mcp/noctusai/node. This is the "per-major targeted override"
#            the retired CVE-2026-33672/33750 entries said was the real fix:
#            1.x and 5.x co-exist in the same tree and are already clean, so
#            a blanket override breaks workbox's 1.x consumer — which is
#            exactly why those two were accepted instead of fixed.
#
# Verified 2026-08-10: with this file EMPTIED ENTIRELY, `trivy fs` at the CI
# config (HIGH/CRITICAL, --ignore-unfixed, skip-dirs projects/archive/
# migratingDB) reports ZERO findings across the tree. The two entries below
# are kept only because they are IMAGE-scan accepts with a live rationale —
# the filesystem gate never saw them either way.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# wheel: Privilege Escalation via malicious wheel file unpacking.
# Non-runtime — `wheel unpack` is never invoked by product code (grep verified).
# Lives in the slim image's /opt/venv, not in any lockfile, so this is inert
# for the `fs` gate; retained for whenever an image scan is wired back up.
# See `accept-with-rationale.md` § `wheel CVE-2026-24049 carried in runtime venv`.
CVE-2026-24049

# jaraco.context: Path traversal via malicious tar archives.
# Non-runtime — `jaraco.context.tarball()` is never invoked by product code.
# Same image-vs-filesystem note as `wheel` above; the shared revisit trigger
# ("scrub non-runtime packages from the builder→runtime copy in the seed
# Dockerfile") is still OPEN — these two are accepted, not formalized.
# See `accept-with-rationale.md` § `jaraco.context CVE-2026-23949 carried in runtime venv`.
CVE-2026-23949
